<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<handout>
    <title>Learning Target 2 Practice</title>

    <p>
        <em>State precisely the definition of an even and odd integer and outline the proof of a statement using these terms.</em>
    </p>

    <p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <p>
                    State the definition of an odd integer.
                    That is, complete the sentence,
                </p>

                <p>
                    An integer <m>n</m> is <term>odd</term> if....
                </p>
            </li>

            <li>
                <p>
                    State the definition of an even integer.
                    That is, complete the sentence,
                </p>

                <p>
                    An integer <m>n</m> is <term>even</term> if....
                </p>
            </li>

            <li>
                <p>
                    Examples with solutions:
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Proposition 2.5 proof on page 250 of your book.
                                (The sum of two odd integers is even.)
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                See solutions on Blackboard!
                            </p>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </li>

            <li>
                <p>
                    Weekly Practice 2 #1:
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                The sum of an even integer and an odd integer is
                                odd.
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                The product of two odd integers is odd.
                            </p>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </li>

            <li>
                <p>
                    Extra Practice: Prove the product of an odd integer and an
                    even integer is even.
                </p>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </p>
</handout>